--
-- Test Description
-- This test applies IP packets of different types where the last data in the
-- packet forces a carry from the final checksum addition. This test is required
-- because the implementation adds the carry in the next cycle, so must look
-- ahead for the final data in the packet to compare against the expected 0xFFFF.
-- All frames in this test should be received successfully.
-- 
-- Functional Coverage
--  * Checks the one's complement addition for the IP checksum
--  * Checks the one's complement addition for the TCP checksum
--  * Checks the one's complement addition for the UDP checksum
-- 
-- Detailed Test Description
--  1. Initialise suitable wait states for the test.
--  2. Check reset values of registers and setup interrupts
--     and then enable receive in 100M mode into a 32-bit DMA data bus.
--  3. Send several IP frames with ethernet encapsulation, which
--     have good IP checksum and are valid UDP or TCP with good checksums
--     and have a carry on the checksum in the final data of the packet.
--
-- Frame 1
--    Carry on final UDP data.
--    Broadcast frame, Valid UDP, odd length, no IP options, no VLAN, no SNAP
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & UDP
--    checksums checked (bits [23:22] = 11) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
--
-- Frame 2
--    Carry on final TCP data.
--    Broadcast frame, Valid TCP, even length, no IP options, no VLAN, no SNAP
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums checked (bits [23:22] = 10) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
--
-- Frame 3
--    Carry on final IP header.
--    Broadcast frame, Valid TCP, even length, no IP options, no VLAN, no SNAP
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums checked (bits [23:22] = 10) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
--
--  4. Check statistics for correct values from above tests.
--
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------


--******************************************************************************
--  1. Initialise suitable wait states for the test.
--******************************************************************************
